WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.422 --> 00:00:03.568
Unit five. Product Design Thinking!

2
00:00:04.526 --> 00:00:08.690
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:12.169
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.219 --> 00:00:16.194
Today we learn about Product Design Thinking. Let's go!

5
00:00:17.502 --> 00:00:21.867
Design thinking. Say it with me. Design thinking!

6
00:00:25.385 --> 00:00:29.518
Empathy map. Say it with me. Empathy map!

7
00:00:33.019 --> 00:00:36.977
Ideation. Say it with me. Ideation!

8
00:00:40.474 --> 00:00:45.268
Rapid prototyping. Say it with me. Rapid prototyping!

9
00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:53.099
User persona. Say it with me. User persona!

10
00:00:56.581 --> 00:01:01.444
Iteration cycle. Say it with me. Iteration cycle!

11
00:01:04.937 --> 00:01:09.871
Minimum viable product. Say it with me. Minimum viable product!

12
00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:17.981
User feedback. Say it with me. User feedback!

13
00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:36.521
Design thinking starts with empathy, often using an empathy map to understand a user persona. Ideation and rapid prototyping help test ideas quickly. Building a minimum viable product and gathering user feedback drives each iteration cycle.

14
00:01:36.571 --> 00:01:39.964
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:40.842 --> 00:01:45.999
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:46.049 --> 00:01:47.199
Ideation!

17
00:01:48.258 --> 00:01:53.587
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:53.637 --> 00:01:55.520
Minimum viable product!

19
00:01:56.402 --> 00:02:04.484
Did you know? Many successful apps started as a very simple minimum viable product before adding more features based on user feedback!

20
00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:06.657
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:07.875 --> 00:02:17.279
Think and answer. Why might starting with a 'minimum viable product' be a smart strategy?

22
00:02:17.329 --> 00:02:18.479
Great answer!

23
00:02:19.586 --> 00:02:24.719
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:24.769 --> 00:02:27.781
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

